---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import WhatsAppLink from '../components/WhatsAppLink.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Parts & Procurement | Equip Solutions Group"
  description="Genuine StarMix SMI plant components, and sourcing for agriculture and hard-to-find parts. Send a number or a photo.">

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap page-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Parts desk</p>
      <h1>Parts &amp; Procurement</h1>
      <p>Genuine SMI components for StarMix plants, and a sourcing desk for everything else &mdash; including the agriculture parts that dead-end at the dealer counter.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="#request">Request a part</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="tel:+15157200800">Call +1 515 720 0800</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="starmix">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Line &middot; StarMix / SMI</p>
        <h2>Volumetric plant parts</h2>
        <p>Genuine SMI components are built by the same manufacturer as the plants and engineered to fit. Many also cross-fit other volumetric brands &mdash; worth asking even if you run a different unit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cats">
        <div class="cat">
          <h4>Electrical Control System</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>DCC data control commander</li>
            <li>Digital counter and data transmitter</li>
            <li>Electrical cabinet and power inverter</li>
            <li>Solenoid valves and manifold</li>
            <li>Magnetic proximity sensors</li>
            <li>Sensor harnesses and limit switches</li>
            <li>Bluetooth thermal printer</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cat">
          <h4>Water System</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Water pumps and impellers</li>
            <li>Lined metal water tanks</li>
            <li>Mechanical seals</li>
            <li>Basket filters</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cat">
          <h4>High-Flow Additive</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>High-flow pumps</li>
            <li>High-volume flowmeters</li>
            <li>Additive tanks</li>
            <li>Pressure gauges to 3,000 PSI</li>
            <li>Relief valves</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cat">
          <h4>Low-Flow Additive</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Low-flow pumps</li>
            <li>Low-volume flowmeters</li>
            <li>Low-flow additive tanks</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cat">
          <h4>Mixing &amp; Conveying</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Mixing augers, 9&Prime; and 12&Prime;</li>
            <li>Conveyor belt assemblies, 18&Prime;</li>
            <li>Drive and wear components</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="cat">
          <h4>Cross-compatibility</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>Fits many competing volumetric units</li>
            <li>Send a photo if unsure of the number</li>
            <li>Bilingual parts support</li>
            <li>Maintenance and rebuild service</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="agriculture">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Independent</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-3);text-transform:uppercase;">Agriculture &amp; hard-to-find parts</h2>
          <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem;">The counter says discontinued. The number superseded twice and the third one is on backorder. That is where this desk earns its keep.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem;color:var(--graphite);">Send whatever you have &mdash; a number stamped in a casting, a photo of the broken piece, or just the make, model and what it does. Old iron is worth keeping in the field, and most of it is still findable if someone is willing to make the calls.</p>
          <ul class="checks" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Tractor and implement parts</strong> across common and obsolete lines.</li>
            <li><strong>Superseded and discontinued numbers</strong> traced to a current equivalent.</li>
            <li><strong>Aftermarket alternatives</strong> when OEM is gone &mdash; with an honest note on quality.</li>
            <li><strong>Wear parts and consumables</strong> sourced in quantity for the season.</li>
            <li><strong>Hydraulics, bearings, seals and drivelines</strong> matched by dimension when the number is unreadable.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ph ph--tall">Photo &mdash; parts on a bench, or a stamped casting number<br>Recommended 900&times;1200</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark on-dark" id="request">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split split--narrow">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Request parts</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-3);text-transform:uppercase;">Send it however you have it</h2>
          <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem;">A part number is ideal. A blurry photo of a casting works too. If the machine is down, say so in the first line and it moves to the front.</p>
          <ul class="checks" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Text a photo</strong> to +1 515 720 0800</li>
            <li><WhatsAppLink /> &mdash; same number, photos of a down machine go to the front</li>
            <li><strong>Email</strong> paul@equipsolutionsgroup.com</li>
            <li><strong>Or fill in the form</strong> on the contact page</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="btn-row">
            <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Open the parts form</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <ul class="checks">
            <li><strong>Machine make, model and serial.</strong> Serial numbers resolve most number conflicts on their own.</li>
            <li><strong>Part number, if legible.</strong> Include every character you can read, even partial.</li>
            <li><strong>Photos.</strong> The part, where it mounts, and any stamped or cast markings.</li>
            <li><strong>Quantity and urgency.</strong> Down machine, scheduled maintenance, or stocking up.</li>
            <li><strong>Ship-to city and state.</strong> So freight is in the quote from the start.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Down machines get called back first"
    body="If a truck or plant is sitting, say so up front. Everything else works in order.">
    <a class="btn" href="tel:+15157200800">Call +1 515 720 0800</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="mailto:paul@equipsolutionsgroup.com">Email the parts desk</a>
  </CtaBand>

</BaseLayout>
